Grist stores an empty \code{Bool} cell as \code{FALSE}, so an \code{NA} written to a \code{Bool}
column is read back as \code{FALSE}. Empty \code{Int}, \code{Numeric}, \code{Date} and
\code{DateTime} cells are read back as \code{NA}.
